{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHeldKeys"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHeldKeyCodes"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useKeyHold"},{"type":"text","value":" to render the current keyboard state. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeyHint"},{"type":"text","value":" to reveal shortcut labels while their modifiers are held."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"read-key-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read key state"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { useHeldKeys, useHeldKeyCodes, useKeyHold, useHotkeyHint } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class KeyStatus extends Component {\n\theld = useHeldKeys(this)\n\tcodes = useHeldKeyCodes(this)\n\tshift = useKeyHold(this, 'Shift')\n\thint = useHotkeyHint(this, 'Mod+S')\n\n\tget keys() { return this.held.value.join(' + ') || 'No keys held' }\n\tget shiftCode() { return this.codes.value.Shift ?? 'Not held' }\n\n\t<template>\n\t\t<p>{{this.keys}}</p>\n\t\t<p>Shift position: {{this.shiftCode}}</p>\n\t\t{{#if this.shift.value}}<button type=\"button\">Delete permanently</button>{{/if}}\n\t\t{{#if this.hint.value}}<kbd>Save</kbd>{{/if}}\n\t</template>\n}","lang":"gts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"useheldkeys","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHeldKeys"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a reactive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".value"},{"type":"text","value":" containing an array of held logical key names, in press order. Names include "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Shift"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Control"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Meta"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"A"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Space"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ArrowUp"},{"type":"text","value":". An empty array means no keys are held."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"useheldkeycodes","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHeldKeyCodes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a reactive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".value"},{"type":"text","value":" containing an object that maps logical names to physical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.code"},{"type":"text","value":" values, such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ Shift: 'ShiftLeft', Control: 'ControlRight' }"},{"type":"text","value":". This lets a debugging display show the physical position associated with a held logical name."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usekeyhold","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useKeyHold"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a reactive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".value"},{"type":"text","value":" containing a boolean for one key. Create separate readers for Shift, Control, Alt, and Meta to show modifier indicators."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".value"},{"type":"text","value":" in a template or reactive getter. Pass a getter for the key argument when it can change."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reading-held-keys-inside-a-stable-callback","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reading held keys inside a stable callback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For an event handler that needs current state without a render subscription, initialize the shared tracker before the keys are pressed and read it inside the callback:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\nconst logHeldKeys = () => {\n\tconsole.log(tracker.getHeldKeys())\n\tconsole.log('Space held:', tracker.isKeyHeld('Space'))\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Saving the result outside the callback captures an earlier snapshot. These imperative reads do not subscribe the component. Do not destroy the shared tracker when your component is removed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a mouse or wheel handler that needs only the event's modifiers, read them directly:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const onWheel = (event: WheelEvent) => {\n\tif (event.ctrlKey) console.log('Wheel with Control modifier')\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A browser may also report "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctrlKey"},{"type":"text","value":" for a trackpad pinch. That does not necessarily mean a physical Control key is held."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hold-to-reveal-ui","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hold-to-reveal UI"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the Shift state to switch between Move to Trash and Delete Permanently actions. The key-state example above shows a button only while Shift is held. The same pattern can reveal alternate menu labels or selection controls."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"keyboard-shortcut-hints","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keyboard shortcut hints"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a binding-aware hint reader rather than hardcoding Meta on every platform. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod+S"},{"type":"text","value":" follows the detected platform. A hint is display state, not a registration or a check that a target is focused."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"debugging-key-display","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging key display"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combine held logical names with the physical-code map. Format a logical name through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formatForDisplay"},{"type":"text","value":" when it is also a valid "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RegisterableHotkey"},{"type":"text","value":", and show the code next to it. Keep physical codes in the diagnostic display even when a layout produces a different logical letter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"modifier-held-shortcut-hints","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modifier-held shortcut hints"}]},{"type":"code","value":"hint = useHotkeyHint(this, 'Alt+Shift+[KeyK]')\n// Read this.hint.value in a template or getter.","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Holding Alt, Shift, or both reveals this hint. Extra Control hides it, as does releasing all modifiers or blurring the window. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph never reveals hints."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ exact: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" to require every binding modifier, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ platform: 'mac' }"},{"type":"text","value":" to resolve "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod"},{"type":"text","value":" explicitly. Supply the same platform used for registration. Combine the result with the action's enabled state. The core equivalent is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a changing binding, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeyHint(this, () => this.binding, () => this.hintOptions)"},{"type":"text","value":". Tracked changes recompute the hint even without a keyboard event."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"platform-quirks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Platform quirks"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"macos-modifier-key-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"macOS modifier key behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"macOS can swallow the keyup event for a non-modifier while a modifier is held. The tracker handles this to keep held state accurate."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"window-blur","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Window blur"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The tracker clears held keys when the browser window loses focus. Keys released while another window is active therefore do not remain stuck in the UI."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"under-the-hood","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Under the hood"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ember subscribes to the core TanStack Store and releases each subscription with its owner. The shared tracker manages keyboard listeners and exposes imperative queries."}]},{"type":"code","value":"tracker.getHeldKeys()\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')\ntracker.isAnyKeyHeld(['Shift', 'Control'])\ntracker.areAllKeysHeld(['Shift', 'Control'])","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Try "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/useHeldKeys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useHeldKeys"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/useKeyHold","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useKeyHold"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and the "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/kitchen-sink","children":[{"type":"text","value":"kitchen sink"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"read-key-state","text":"Read key state","level":2},{"id":"useheldkeys","text":"useHeldKeys","level":2},{"id":"useheldkeycodes","text":"useHeldKeyCodes","level":2},{"id":"usekeyhold","text":"useKeyHold","level":2},{"id":"common-patterns","text":"Common patterns","level":2},{"id":"reading-held-keys-inside-a-stable-callback","text":"Reading held keys inside a stable callback","level":3},{"id":"hold-to-reveal-ui","text":"Hold-to-reveal UI","level":3},{"id":"keyboard-shortcut-hints","text":"Keyboard shortcut hints","level":3},{"id":"debugging-key-display","text":"Debugging key display","level":3},{"id":"modifier-held-shortcut-hints","text":"Modifier-held shortcut hints","level":2},{"id":"platform-quirks","text":"Platform quirks","level":2},{"id":"macos-modifier-key-behavior","text":"macOS modifier key behavior","level":3},{"id":"window-blur","text":"Window blur","level":3},{"id":"under-the-hood","text":"Under the hood","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nUse `useHeldKeys`, `useHeldKeyCodes`, and `useKeyHold` to render the current keyboard state. Use `useHotkeyHint` to reveal shortcut labels while their modifiers are held.\n\n## Read key state\n\n\n```gts\nimport Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { useHeldKeys, useHeldKeyCodes, useKeyHold, useHotkeyHint } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class KeyStatus extends Component {\n\theld = useHeldKeys(this)\n\tcodes = useHeldKeyCodes(this)\n\tshift = useKeyHold(this, 'Shift')\n\thint = useHotkeyHint(this, 'Mod+S')\n\n\tget keys() { return this.held.value.join(' + ') || 'No keys held' }\n\tget shiftCode() { return this.codes.value.Shift ?? 'Not held' }\n\n\t<template>\n\t\t<p>{{this.keys}}</p>\n\t\t<p>Shift position: {{this.shiftCode}}</p>\n\t\t{{#if this.shift.value}}<button type=\"button\">Delete permanently</button>{{/if}}\n\t\t{{#if this.hint.value}}<kbd>Save</kbd>{{/if}}\n\t</template>\n}\n```\n\n## `useHeldKeys`\n\nReturns a reactive `.value` containing an array of held logical key names, in press order. Names include `Shift`, `Control`, `Meta`, `A`, `Space`, and `ArrowUp`. An empty array means no keys are held.\n\n## `useHeldKeyCodes`\n\nReturns a reactive `.value` containing an object that maps logical names to physical `event.code` values, such as `{ Shift: 'ShiftLeft', Control: 'ControlRight' }`. This lets a debugging display show the physical position associated with a held logical name.\n\n## `useKeyHold`\n\nReturns a reactive `.value` containing a boolean for one key. Create separate readers for Shift, Control, Alt, and Meta to show modifier indicators.\n\nRead `.value` in a template or reactive getter. Pass a getter for the key argument when it can change.\n\n## Common patterns\n\n### Reading held keys inside a stable callback\n\nFor an event handler that needs current state without a render subscription, initialize the shared tracker before the keys are pressed and read it inside the callback:\n\n```ts\nimport { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\nconst logHeldKeys = () => {\n\tconsole.log(tracker.getHeldKeys())\n\tconsole.log('Space held:', tracker.isKeyHeld('Space'))\n}\n```\n\nSaving the result outside the callback captures an earlier snapshot. These imperative reads do not subscribe the component. Do not destroy the shared tracker when your component is removed.\n\nFor a mouse or wheel handler that needs only the event's modifiers, read them directly:\n\n```ts\nconst onWheel = (event: WheelEvent) => {\n\tif (event.ctrlKey) console.log('Wheel with Control modifier')\n}\n```\n\nA browser may also report `ctrlKey` for a trackpad pinch. That does not necessarily mean a physical Control key is held.\n\n### Hold-to-reveal UI\n\nUse the Shift state to switch between Move to Trash and Delete Permanently actions. The key-state example above shows a button only while Shift is held. The same pattern can reveal alternate menu labels or selection controls.\n\n### Keyboard shortcut hints\n\nUse a binding-aware hint reader rather than hardcoding Meta on every platform. `Mod+S` follows the detected platform. A hint is display state, not a registration or a check that a target is focused.\n\n### Debugging key display\n\nCombine held logical names with the physical-code map. Format a logical name through `formatForDisplay` when it is also a valid `RegisterableHotkey`, and show the code next to it. Keep physical codes in the diagnostic display even when a layout produces a different logical letter.\n\n## Modifier-held shortcut hints\n\n\n```ts\nhint = useHotkeyHint(this, 'Alt+Shift+[KeyK]')\n// Read this.hint.value in a template or getter.\n```\n\nHolding Alt, Shift, or both reveals this hint. Extra Control hides it, as does releasing all modifiers or blurring the window. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph never reveals hints.\n\nPass `{ exact: true }` to require every binding modifier, or `{ platform: 'mac' }` to resolve `Mod` explicitly. Supply the same platform used for registration. Combine the result with the action's enabled state. The core equivalent is `matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)`.\n\nFor a changing binding, use `useHotkeyHint(this, () => this.binding, () => this.hintOptions)`. Tracked changes recompute the hint even without a keyboard event.\n\n## Platform quirks\n\n### macOS modifier key behavior\n\nmacOS can swallow the keyup event for a non-modifier while a modifier is held. The tracker handles this to keep held state accurate.\n\n### Window blur\n\nThe tracker clears held keys when the browser window loses focus. Keys released while another window is active therefore do not remain stuck in the UI.\n\n## Under the hood\n\nEmber subscribes to the core TanStack Store and releases each subscription with its owner. The shared tracker manages keyboard listeners and exposes imperative queries.\n\n```ts\ntracker.getHeldKeys()\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')\ntracker.isAnyKeyHeld(['Shift', 'Control'])\ntracker.areAllKeysHeld(['Shift', 'Control'])\n```\n\nTry [useHeldKeys](../examples/useHeldKeys), [useKeyHold](../examples/useKeyHold), and the [kitchen sink](../examples/kitchen-sink).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Key State Tracking Guide\nid: key-state-tracking\n---\n\nUse `useHeldKeys`, `useHeldKeyCodes`, and `useKeyHold` to render the current keyboard state. Use `useHotkeyHint` to reveal shortcut labels while their modifiers are held.\n\n## Read key state\n\n\n```gts\nimport Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { useHeldKeys, useHeldKeyCodes, useKeyHold, useHotkeyHint } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class KeyStatus extends Component {\n\theld = useHeldKeys(this)\n\tcodes = useHeldKeyCodes(this)\n\tshift = useKeyHold(this, 'Shift')\n\thint = useHotkeyHint(this, 'Mod+S')\n\n\tget keys() { return this.held.value.join(' + ') || 'No keys held' }\n\tget shiftCode() { return this.codes.value.Shift ?? 'Not held' }\n\n\t<template>\n\t\t<p>{{this.keys}}</p>\n\t\t<p>Shift position: {{this.shiftCode}}</p>\n\t\t{{#if this.shift.value}}<button type=\"button\">Delete permanently</button>{{/if}}\n\t\t{{#if this.hint.value}}<kbd>Save</kbd>{{/if}}\n\t</template>\n}\n```\n\n## `useHeldKeys`\n\nReturns a reactive `.value` containing an array of held logical key names, in press order. Names include `Shift`, `Control`, `Meta`, `A`, `Space`, and `ArrowUp`. An empty array means no keys are held.\n\n## `useHeldKeyCodes`\n\nReturns a reactive `.value` containing an object that maps logical names to physical `event.code` values, such as `{ Shift: 'ShiftLeft', Control: 'ControlRight' }`. This lets a debugging display show the physical position associated with a held logical name.\n\n## `useKeyHold`\n\nReturns a reactive `.value` containing a boolean for one key. Create separate readers for Shift, Control, Alt, and Meta to show modifier indicators.\n\nRead `.value` in a template or reactive getter. Pass a getter for the key argument when it can change.\n\n## Common patterns\n\n### Reading held keys inside a stable callback\n\nFor an event handler that needs current state without a render subscription, initialize the shared tracker before the keys are pressed and read it inside the callback:\n\n```ts\nimport { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\nconst logHeldKeys = () => {\n\tconsole.log(tracker.getHeldKeys())\n\tconsole.log('Space held:', tracker.isKeyHeld('Space'))\n}\n```\n\nSaving the result outside the callback captures an earlier snapshot. These imperative reads do not subscribe the component. Do not destroy the shared tracker when your component is removed.\n\nFor a mouse or wheel handler that needs only the event's modifiers, read them directly:\n\n```ts\nconst onWheel = (event: WheelEvent) => {\n\tif (event.ctrlKey) console.log('Wheel with Control modifier')\n}\n```\n\nA browser may also report `ctrlKey` for a trackpad pinch. That does not necessarily mean a physical Control key is held.\n\n### Hold-to-reveal UI\n\nUse the Shift state to switch between Move to Trash and Delete Permanently actions. The key-state example above shows a button only while Shift is held. The same pattern can reveal alternate menu labels or selection controls.\n\n### Keyboard shortcut hints\n\nUse a binding-aware hint reader rather than hardcoding Meta on every platform. `Mod+S` follows the detected platform. A hint is display state, not a registration or a check that a target is focused.\n\n### Debugging key display\n\nCombine held logical names with the physical-code map. Format a logical name through `formatForDisplay` when it is also a valid `RegisterableHotkey`, and show the code next to it. Keep physical codes in the diagnostic display even when a layout produces a different logical letter.\n\n## Modifier-held shortcut hints\n\n\n```ts\nhint = useHotkeyHint(this, 'Alt+Shift+[KeyK]')\n// Read this.hint.value in a template or getter.\n```\n\nHolding Alt, Shift, or both reveals this hint. Extra Control hides it, as does releasing all modifiers or blurring the window. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph never reveals hints.\n\nPass `{ exact: true }` to require every binding modifier, or `{ platform: 'mac' }` to resolve `Mod` explicitly. Supply the same platform used for registration. Combine the result with the action's enabled state. The core equivalent is `matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)`.\n\nFor a changing binding, use `useHotkeyHint(this, () => this.binding, () => this.hintOptions)`. Tracked changes recompute the hint even without a keyboard event.\n\n## Platform quirks\n\n### macOS modifier key behavior\n\nmacOS can swallow the keyup event for a non-modifier while a modifier is held. The tracker handles this to keep held state accurate.\n\n### Window blur\n\nThe tracker clears held keys when the browser window loses focus. Keys released while another window is active therefore do not remain stuck in the UI.\n\n## Under the hood\n\nEmber subscribes to the core TanStack Store and releases each subscription with its owner. The shared tracker manages keyboard listeners and exposes imperative queries.\n\n```ts\ntracker.getHeldKeys()\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')\ntracker.isAnyKeyHeld(['Shift', 'Control'])\ntracker.areAllKeysHeld(['Shift', 'Control'])\n```\n\nTry [useHeldKeys](../examples/useHeldKeys), [useKeyHold](../examples/useKeyHold), and the [kitchen sink](../examples/kitchen-sink).\n"}
